# JVN Runtime Demo Prologue + Puppeteer Timeline Showcase

@scenario runtime_demo_prologue
@character narrator "Narrator"
@character hero "Hero"
@character guide "Guide"
@background classroom game/images/backgrounds/classroom_day.png
@background sunset game/images/backgrounds/sunset_street.png

@label start
[bg classroom]
[transition fade 400]
[set playerName Player]
[set courage 0]

Narrator: Welcome to {b}JVN Runtime{/b}.
Narrator: This build now includes a heavy inline timeline showcase to demonstrate Puppeteer-style choreography.
Hero: I'm {color=#4a9eff}${playerName}{/color}. Pick a route.
[show hero center neutral]

> Full Puppeteer timeline showcase -> puppeteer_showcase
> Classic branching mini-tour -> tour
> Skip to ending -> speedrun

@label puppeteer_showcase
[bg classroom]
[transition fade 400]
[show hero left neutral]
[show guide right smile]
Narrator: We start with baseline placement and then run a lot of timeline animation beats.

timeline {
  move "hero" {
    x: 120
    y: 410
    dur: 0
  }
  move "guide" {
    x: 260
    y: 410
    dur: 0
  }
}
[wait 50]

timeline {
  move "hero" {
    x: 900
    y: 410
    dur: 850
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  move "guide" {
    x: 1040
    y: 410
    dur: 850
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
}
[wait 900]

Hero: Entry sequence done. Next up: layered movement + rotation.

timeline {
  move "hero" {
    x: 620
    y: 400
    dur: 420
    easing: ease_in_out_cubic
  }
  rotate "hero" {
    angle: -8
    dur: 420
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  wait 120
  scale "hero" {
    x: 1.18
    y: 0.86
    dur: 170
    easing: ease_out_quad
  }
  wait 190
  scale "hero" {
    x: 1.0
    y: 1.0
    dur: 180
    easing: ease_in_out_quad
  }
}
[wait 850]

timeline {
  move "hero" {
    x: 420
    y: 410
    dur: 320
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  rotate "hero" {
    angle: 0
    dur: 320
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
}
[wait 380]

Guide: Now watch pivot-origin control and chained rotations.

timeline {
  pivot "guide" {
    ox: 0.5
    oy: 0.9
    dur: 220
    easing: ease_out_quad
  }
  rotate "guide" {
    angle: 12
    dur: 220
    easing: ease_out_back
  }
  wait 220
  rotate "guide" {
    angle: -10
    dur: 240
    easing: ease_in_out_quad
  }
  wait 240
  rotate "guide" {
    angle: 0
    dur: 240
    easing: ease_out_quad
  }
}
[wait 760]

Narrator: Camera timeline tracks are also supported.

timeline {
  cameraMove {
    x: 95
    y: -12
    dur: 700
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  cameraZoom {
    zoom: 1.12
    dur: 700
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
}
[wait 760]

timeline {
  cameraMove {
    x: 0
    y: 0
    dur: 520
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  cameraZoom {
    zoom: 1.0
    dur: 520
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
}
[wait 560]

Narrator: We can transition background and keep timeline choreography going.
[transition crossfade 700 sunset]
[wait 740]

timeline {
  move "hero" {
    x: 480
    y: 415
    dur: 460
    easing: ease_in_out_quad
  }
  move "guide" {
    x: 820
    y: 415
    dur: 460
    easing: ease_in_out_quad
  }
}
[wait 520]

timeline {
  move "hero" {
    x: 610
    y: 400
    dur: 250
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  move "guide" {
    x: 690
    y: 400
    dur: 250
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  wait 260
  move "hero" {
    x: 430
    y: 410
    dur: 250
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  move "guide" {
    x: 870
    y: 410
    dur: 250
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  wait 260
  move "hero" {
    x: 560
    y: 405
    dur: 260
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  move "guide" {
    x: 740
    y: 405
    dur: 260
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
}
[wait 900]

Narrator: Fades can do spotlight beats.

timeline {
  fade "guide" {
    alpha: 0.25
    dur: 280
    easing: ease_in_out_quad
  }
}
[wait 320]

timeline {
  fade "guide" {
    alpha: 1.0
    dur: 300
    easing: ease_out_quad
  }
}
[wait 340]

timeline {
  fade "hero" {
    alpha: 0.35
    dur: 260
    easing: ease_in_out_quad
  }
}
[wait 300]

timeline {
  fade "hero" {
    alpha: 1.0
    dur: 280
    easing: ease_out_quad
  }
}
[wait 320]

Guide: Finale combo: move + rotate + scale + camera at once.

timeline {
  move "hero" {
    x: 470
    y: 395
    dur: 620
    easing: ease_in_out_cubic
  }
  move "guide" {
    x: 860
    y: 395
    dur: 620
    easing: ease_in_out_cubic
  }
  rotate "hero" {
    angle: -7
    dur: 620
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  rotate "guide" {
    angle: 7
    dur: 620
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  scale "hero" {
    x: 1.14
    y: 1.14
    dur: 620
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  scale "guide" {
    x: 1.14
    y: 1.14
    dur: 620
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  cameraMove {
    x: 40
    y: -8
    dur: 620
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  cameraZoom {
    zoom: 1.08
    dur: 620
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
}
[wait 680]

timeline {
  move "hero" {
    x: 560
    y: 405
    dur: 500
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  move "guide" {
    x: 740
    y: 405
    dur: 500
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  rotate "hero" {
    angle: 0
    dur: 500
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  rotate "guide" {
    angle: 0
    dur: 500
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  scale "hero" {
    x: 1.0
    y: 1.0
    dur: 500
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  scale "guide" {
    x: 1.0
    y: 1.0
    dur: 500
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  cameraMove {
    x: 0
    y: 0
    dur: 500
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  cameraZoom {
    zoom: 1.0
    dur: 500
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
}
[wait 560]

Narrator: That was a full in-script timeline showcase using the same action family Puppeteer exports.
[jump ending]

@label tour
[inc courage 1]
[show guide right smile]
Guide: Great. Here's {wave}smooth motion{/wave} plus a {shake}dramatic hit{/shake}.
[screen flash 0.35 160 1 1 1]
Narrator: Choice conditions can depend on variables, and timelines can be mixed into any branch.

> Step forward confidently [if courage >= 1] -> brave
> Stay cautious -> cautious

@label brave
[transition crossfade 700 sunset]
timeline {
  move "hero" {
    x: 600
    y: 400
    dur: 420
    easing: ease_out_back
  }
  scale "hero" {
    x: 1.1
    y: 1.1
    dur: 420
    easing: ease_out_quad
  }
}
[wait 480]
Hero: Nice. This is where your own chapter can begin.
Narrator: Replace this script with your story and your assets.
[jump ending]

@label cautious
timeline {
  cameraMove {
    x: -40
    y: 0
    dur: 380
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
  cameraZoom {
    zoom: 0.96
    dur: 380
    easing: ease_in_out_sine
  }
}
[wait 430]
timeline {
  cameraMove {
    x: 0
    y: 0
    dur: 340
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
  cameraZoom {
    zoom: 1.0
    dur: 340
    easing: ease_out_sine
  }
}
[wait 390]
Hero: Let's keep it simple and move on.
Narrator: You can expand this scene in the editor at any time.
[jump ending]

@label speedrun
Narrator: Speedrun accepted.
[jump ending]

@label ending
Narrator: {wave}The End{/wave} - now build your VN.
[end]
